}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4{t}^{3/2}+4{t}^{2}+5),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-4{t}^{2}+t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨6{t}^{1/2}+8t,\\,3{t}^{2}-8t+1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to compute the acceleration vector, we differentiate the velocity vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a & =\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t} \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}t}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6{t}^{1/2}+8t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3{t}^{2}-8t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{-1/2}+8,\\,6t-8⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the acceleration at time $t=1,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(1) & =⟨3(1)^{-1/2}+8,\\,6(1)-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+8,\\,6-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨11,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to find the magnitude of the acceleration, we compute $|a(1)|:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a(1)| & =|⟨11,\\,-2⟩| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{11}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092189 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299839 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092189 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299843 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092189 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299903 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092189 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299904 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092189 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299905 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092189 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299906 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092189 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299907 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092189 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299908 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092189 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299909 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092190 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299910 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092190 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299911 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186092190 1038 #edb/ref 17592186299915 13194139533412 17592186045585 t