92186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299582 1071 "Consider the expression $f(x,y)=-5{x}^{2}{y}^{4}.$ Fill the table with appropriate sign of $f(x,y)$ as shown below.\n\n| $y>0$ | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299582 1072 #uuid "47ec2ccb-ee9a-5a26-9439-3630e85191ad" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299582 1074 "Notice that $f(x,y)$ equals zero when $x=0$ and $y=0.$ These lines divide the $xy$-plane into four regions, as shown below.\n\n![](images/5f/5fd85410238231152b6f905921f594af15293d6efc54b0b1ce558131a05bf6ee.png)\n\nTo determine the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region, we pick four test points, one for each region.\n\n![](images/e9/e95107f16eb80a06cd172c30ec78992838f974a91f9f2fa17b7c8ac77125c438.png)\n\nNext, we calculate the sign of $f(x,y)$ in each region using a sign table:\n\n|  | Test point | $-5{x}^{2}$ | ${y}^{4}$ | $f(x,y)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Top-Left | $(-1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Top-Right | $(1,1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Left | $(-1,-1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n| Bottom-Right | $(1,-1)$ | $-$ | $+$ | $-$ |\n\n \n\nUsing the *last* column of the table above, we get the following picture:\n\n![](images/11/11b3996767c556af3e377b9a2f72971dffe3d177489a7682b62b59fdef0dcb51.png)\n\nFinally, we fill in the required sign table.\n\n| $y>0$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y<0$ | $-$ | $-$ |\n|  | $x<0$ | $x>0$ |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299583 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298704 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299583 1069 "q-317286" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299583 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299583 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-{6}^{x}-1?$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299583 1072 #uuid "e3041399-5257-5519-a830-54bfb4da44b4" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299583 1074 "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y={6}^{x}.$\n\n![](images/d9/d96daead4646355f2cf0887afc9ddb9b51637d9c54f4f61870cc714ebd5992a0.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-{6}^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/39/3957fdd6a1ff8ece5a02eed85cc6f9941ef797ea8d6f2cedf2c322bd9393cdb1.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $1$ unit down to give $y=-{6}^{x}-1.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,-2)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-1.$\n\n![](images/80/8088ef67878739dc50544bfa9f1e21970a595c9e61bab4feb67de708b416378a.png)" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299584 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299060 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299584 1069 "q-317288" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299584 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299584 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-{5}^{x}+4?$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299584 1072 #uuid "74fb21d8-cb80-5a04-9e4d-003c004a6f4b" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299584 1074 "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y={5}^{x}.$\n\n![](images/09/09798cb8c62aabe483490ad24f4c13918138c4292ffb19a8d6612ab4efe18497.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-{5}^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $4$ units up to give $y=-{5}^{x}+4.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,3)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=4.$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299585 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299105 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299585 1069 "q-317294" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299585 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299585 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x}+4?$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299585 1072 #uuid "f5a2bf88-da34-5e50-afc7-6bfeb2513dfb" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299585 1074 "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y={(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x}.$\n\n![](images/d6/d67114a9865ca54cdf14798e779cfa9c00e71598ba652d6fccdcf686f86e20ef.png)\n\n \n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,1)$ to $(0,-1)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/d6/d6dcae76f7fe89188ef449c817f7e7af48c25763077d1daee9626d2f26b1a78a.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $4$ units up to give $y=-{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x}+4.$ The point $(0,-1)$ moves to $(0,3)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=4.$\n\n![](images/52/529dfc1ef1bc6f0ff58addca6cf27c5039a6cf18c5a307c06a153a3d56040ede.png)" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299586 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298909 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299586 1069 "q-317302" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299586 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299586 1071 "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨\\sqrt{7},-2,5⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨\\sqrt{7},3,-1⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299586 1072 #uuid "e756bda8-091e-58df-91a3-7d6c4fd6790c" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299586 1074 "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨\\sqrt{7},-2,5⟩\\cdot ⟨\\sqrt{7},3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =(\\sqrt{7})(\\sqrt{7})+(-2)(3)+(5)(-1) \\\\  & =7-6-5 \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299587 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299342 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299587 1069 "q-317303" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299587 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299587 1071 "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨-\\sqrt{8},\\,4,\\,-3⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨\\sqrt{8},\\,-1,\\,2⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299587 1072 #uuid "dcaa5f3b-4be2-5705-929a-5ba642430c92" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299587 1074 "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨-\\sqrt{8},\\,4,\\,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨\\sqrt{8},\\,-1,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =(-\\sqrt{8})(\\sqrt{8})+(4)(-1)+(-3)(2) \\\\  & =-8-4-6 \\\\  & =-18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299588 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298952 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299588 1069 "q-317304" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299588 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299588 1071 "Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ given that $a=⟨0,\\,5,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩$ and $b\\times c=⟨7,\\,-2,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩.$\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299588 1072 #uuid "47306bb8-b679-542e-9111-9cf80b931f6e" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299588 1074 "Substituting given vectors into the formula for the scalar triple product, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨0,\\,5,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩\\cdot ⟨7,\\,-2,\\,\\sqrt{11}⟩ \\\\  & =(0)(7)+(5)(-2)+(\\sqrt{11})(\\sqrt{11}) \\\\  & =0-10+11 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299589 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299310 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299589 1069 "q-317312" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299589 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299589 1071 "Let $a=⟨2,-1,3⟩$, $b=⟨0,4,1⟩$ and $c=⟨-2,1,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299589 1072 #uuid "e7f80b43-a2f5-515b-92f2-1141b2bd6cfe" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299589 1074 "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\,(4\\cdot 5-1\\cdot 1)\\,-\\,(-1)\\,(0\\cdot 5-1\\cdot (-2))\\,+\\,3\\,(0\\cdot 1-4\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =2\\,(19)\\,-\\,(-1)\\,(2)\\,+\\,3\\,(8) \\\\  & =38+2+24 \\\\  & =64.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299590 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299299 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299590 1069 "q-317315" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299590 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299590 1071 "Let $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨4,0,1⟩$ and $c=⟨-2,-1,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299590 1072 #uuid "4cbf30f6-1867-5976-9eac-2960f6231475" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299590 1074 "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(0\\cdot 5-1\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,2\\,(4\\cdot 5-1\\cdot (-2))\\,+\\,3\\,(4\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =1\\,(1)\\,-\\,2\\,(22)\\,+\\,3\\,(-4) \\\\  & =1-44-12 \\\\  & =-55.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299591 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298838 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299591 1069 "q-317316" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299591 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299591 1071 "Let $a=⟨0,2,5⟩$, $b=⟨3,1,0⟩$ and $c=⟨4,-1,-2⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299591 1072 #uuid "2672a60f-3785-5ec9-9526-2daad7a5333b" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299591 1074 "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,5\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\,(1\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,2\\,(3\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 4)\\,+\\,5\\,(3\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =0(-2)\\,-\\,2\\,(-6)\\,+\\,5\\,(-7) \\\\  & =0+12-35 \\\\  & =-23.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299592 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299016 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299592 1069 "q-317317" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299592 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299592 1071 "Let $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨4,0,-2⟩$ and $c=⟨5,6,1⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299592 1072 #uuid "e752a1da-5c2f-551a-a669-66eee02c7b08" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299592 1074 "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(0\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 6)\\,-\\,2\\,(4\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 5)\\,+\\,3\\,(4\\cdot 6-0\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =1\\,(12)\\,-\\,2\\,(14)\\,+\\,3\\,(24) \\\\  & =12-28+72 \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299593 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299367 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299593 1069 "q-317319" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299593 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299593 1071 "Let $a=⟨2,1,3⟩$, $b=⟨1,4,0⟩$ and $c=⟨6,-1,2⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299593 1072 #uuid "ffaceba3-4514-5d9f-9674-fd0da3b7e455" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299593 1074 "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\,(4\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-1))\\,-\\,1\\,(1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 6)\\,+\\,3\\,(1\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =2\\,(8)\\,-\\,1\\,(2)\\,+\\,3\\,(-25) \\\\  & =16-2-75 \\\\  & =-61.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299594 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299153 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299594 1069 "q-317320" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299594 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299594 1071 "Let $a=⟨1,0,2⟩$, $b=⟨3,1,0⟩$ and $c=⟨4,2,5⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299594 1072 #uuid "e8459484-168d-53bc-8fac-703a96f7dc80" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299594 1074 "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\,(1\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 2)\\,-\\,0\\,(3\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 4)\\,+\\,2\\,(3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =1\\,(5)\\,-\\,0\\,(15)\\,+\\,2\\,(2) \\\\  & =5+0+4 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299595 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298917 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299595 1069 "q-317322" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299595 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299595 1071 "Let $a=⟨2,1,0⟩$, $b=⟨0,3,4⟩$ and $c=⟨5,2,1⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299595 1072 #uuid "c1b3c364-d315-5da6-9fc0-ab4b2a4285e2" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299595 1074 "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\,(3\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 2)\\,-\\,1\\,(0\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 5)\\,+\\,0\\,(0\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 5) \\\\  & =2\\,(-5)\\,-\\,1\\,(-20)\\,+\\,0\\,(-15) \\\\  & =-10+20+0 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299596 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299273 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299596 1069 "q-317325" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299596 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299596 1071 "Let $a=⟨-1,-2,3⟩$, $b=⟨4,-1,-2⟩$ and $c=⟨1,2,-3⟩.$ Find $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ using a determinant.\n\n$a\\cdot (b\\times c)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299596 1072 #uuid "86560436-5dd3-5177-80a9-3ddb91ccbf81" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299596 1074 "Remember that the scalar triple product $a\\cdot (b\\times c)$ is just the determinant of the matrix whose rows are given by $a,$ $b,$ and $c.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\,-\\,(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|\\,+\\,3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-1)\\,((-1)(-3)-(-2)\\cdot 2)\\,-\\,(-2)\\,(4\\cdot (-3)-(-2)\\cdot 1)\\,+\\,3\\,(4\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1) \\\\  & =(-1)\\,(7)\\,-\\,(-2)\\,(-10)\\,+\\,3\\,(9) \\\\  & =-7-20+27 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299597 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298872 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299597 1069 "q-317335" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299597 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299597 1071 "Calculate $det(R)$ given that\n$R=[\\begin{aligned}8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(R)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299597 1072 #uuid "52b70b4e-c944-5a6c-9fb5-10e8bb1b8364" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299597 1074 "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(R) & =|\\begin{aligned}8 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(8)(4)-(-5)(3) \\\\  & =32+15 \\\\  & =47.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299598 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299163 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299598 1069 "q-317336" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299598 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299598 1071 "Calculate $det(S)$ given that\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(S)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299598 1072 #uuid "51e6ce71-0f6b-5ca6-9047-0832d38b3af3" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299598 1074 "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2)(3)-(4)(1) \\\\  & =6-4 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299599 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299343 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299599 1069 "q-317342" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299599 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299599 1071 "Calculate $det(S)$ given that\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(S)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299599 1072 #uuid "cd3c7419-67b1-5120-a5e4-6bd19d8d0a71" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299599 1074 "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}6 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(6)(7)-(-2)(5) \\\\  & =42+10 \\\\  & =52.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299600 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299480 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299600 1069 "q-317343" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299600 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299600 1071 "Find $b\\cdot (c\\times a),$ if $b\\times c=⟨4,-1,6⟩$ and $a=⟨2,3,-1⟩.$\n\n$b\\cdot (c\\times a)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299600 1072 #uuid "6ef37e01-1bf6-55b3-89e8-cc90cafd078c" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299600 1074 "First, we compute the triple scalar product \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =⟨2,3,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-1,6⟩ \\\\  & =2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-1)+(-1)\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =8-3-6 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we swap $a$ and $b$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (a\\times c)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand again we swap $a$ and $c$ to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}b\\cdot (c\\times a)=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299601 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299117 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299601 1069 "q-317359" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299601 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299601 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-2{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x}-6?$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299601 1072 #uuid "4221ea3f-4ea4-5360-8022-7beb92f1bc9e" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299601 1074 "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y=2{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x}.$\n\n![](images/9b/9b254387cd5a117e9dbc470b4f71d56399cb8cde9bb5b83b12f956b538383e61.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-2{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x}.$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,2)$ to $(0,-2)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/e4/e46a5ad8d2f51bc5112c960167879ff352e372bde573834d5394118448a8224c.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $6$ units down to give $y=-2{(\\frac{1}{5})}^{x}-6.$ The point $(0,-2)$ moves to $(0,-8)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-6.$\n\n![](images/4a/4a360d7b90f2c2ea9b561ad53626682ed2b2b2f7459ab8c7bdafe8c02486c9c5.png)" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299602 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298676 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299602 1069 "q-317367" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299602 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299602 1071 "Calculate $det(D)$ given that\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(D)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299602 1072 #uuid "e6ca014c-b5cb-5825-95b8-87e00a3142c6" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299602 1074 "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5} & -3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}\\cdot 2-(-3)\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299603 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299435 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299603 1069 "q-317368" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299603 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299603 1071 "Calculate $det(E)$ given that\n$E=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4} & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(E)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299603 1072 #uuid "a27ba74d-67e7-552a-808b-c86c1ab2858a" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299603 1074 "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(E) & =|\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4} & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}-10 \\\\  & =-\\frac{37}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299604 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299363 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299604 1069 "q-317372" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299604 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299604 1071 "Calculate $det(D)$ given that\n$D=[\\begin{aligned}3x & 2y \\\\ -5 & x\\end{aligned}].$\n\n$det(D)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299604 1072 #uuid "5cb8c1aa-faf5-5b19-b22a-04f7e16807fe" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299604 1074 "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}3x & 2y \\\\ -5 & x\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3x\\cdot x-2y\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}+10y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299605 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298970 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299605 1069 "q-317374" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299605 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299605 1071 "Evaluate the determinant:\n\n$|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}|=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299605 1072 #uuid "9aa98f1a-30c2-558c-875f-c99582477892" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299605 1074 "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & y \\\\ 4 & \\sqrt{6}\\end{aligned}| & =\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}-y\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6-4y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299606 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298722 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299606 1069 "q-317377" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299606 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299606 1071 "If\n    $D=[\\begin{aligned}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$\\text{det}(D)=-11,$ determine the value of $m.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299606 1072 #uuid "1e3ffcd6-7f26-5f4f-8230-33ae44d7f744" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299606 1074 "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}(D) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & m \\\\ 3 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5-m\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =10-3m.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(D)=-11,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D) & =-11 \\\\ 10-3m & =-11 \\\\ -3m & =-21 \\\\ m & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299607 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299442 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299607 1069 "q-317382" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299607 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299607 1071 "If\n$U=[\\begin{aligned}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(U)=-6$, what is the value of $r?$\n\n$r=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299607 1072 #uuid "d0f61095-530a-54e2-bb79-353fa0efed39" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299607 1074 "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =|\\begin{aligned}1+r & 2-r \\\\ -5 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1+r)\\cdot 4-(2-r)\\cdot (-5) \\\\  & =4+4r+10-5r \\\\  & =14-r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(U)=-6,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(U) & =-6 \\\\ 14-r & =-6 \\\\ -r & =-20 \\\\ r & =20.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299608 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298694 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299608 1069 "q-317385" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299608 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299608 1071 "If\n$S=[\\begin{aligned}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{aligned}]$\nand $det(S)=25,$ what is the value of $s?$\n\n$s=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299608 1072 #uuid "6e22859c-f056-5995-96a3-08af912796b8" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299608 1074 "For a $2\\times 2$ matrix, the determinant is given by the formula\n\n$$\n|\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}|=ad-bc.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =|\\begin{aligned}3+s & 2s \\\\ -4 & 3-s\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(3+s)(3-s)-2s(-4) \\\\  & =9-{s}^{2}+8s \\\\  & =-{s}^{2}+8s+9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $det(S)=25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(S) & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s+9 & =25 \\\\ -{s}^{2}+8s-16 & =0 \\\\ {s}^{2}-8s+16 & =0 \\\\ (s-4)^{2} & =0 \\\\ s & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299609 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299195 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299609 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299207 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299609 1069 "q-317429" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299609 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299609 1071 "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 5 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$\n\n| $v=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299609 1072 #uuid "b6998f43-65a5-5cc0-add9-e811dcb25991" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299609 1074 "From the given information, we have \n\n$$\nT\\cdot v=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe need to reverse the action of the matrix $T.$ So, we multiply the above equation by ${T}^{-1},$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1}\\cdot T\\cdot v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to calculate the inverse of $T$, which is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{12+10}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the original vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & ={T}^{-1}\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{22}[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 19\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{11} \\\\ \\frac{19}{22}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299610 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299434 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299610 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299446 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299610 1069 "q-317431" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299610 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299610 1071 "The vector $v$ in the plane is mapped to the vector $[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ whose matrix $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -5 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat is the original vector $v?$\n\n| $v=\\,