 |  |  |  |\n|  | $x$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-10$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n." 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299625 1072 #uuid "042fab86-9bc5-5bac-af22-a67d3b6956f7" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299625 1074 "First, we organize the system so that it’s in the correct order and both $x$ and $y$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+0y=4 \\\\ 0x+y=-10\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299626 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299200 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299626 1069 "q-317541" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299626 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299626 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y=-2({3}^{x})+1?$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299626 1072 #uuid "6f6078fd-cb88-50b6-8d24-b8073d12e091" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299626 1074 "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y=2({3}^{x}).$\n\n![](images/7a/7a11b33423337a8d7f0222e1586753d62374f3d8b3eca02cccadd99e50b9eb1b.png)\n\n- Reflect it on the $x$-axis to give $y=-2({3}^{x}).$ The $y$-intercept moves from $(0,2)$ to $(0,-2)$ but the horizontal asymptote stays at $y=0.$\n\n![](images/53/53aedebd12a8f1138efcc9e9815dba7cf15d869da4f321274f6b0cd367e28cac.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $1$ unit up to give $y=-2({3}^{x})+1.$ The point $(0,-2)$ moves to $(0,-1)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=1.$\n\n![](images/d8/d862abef96431d8165d0b6c1fd76419597f828824fab1bf88eb4ccba5e6dfda8.png)" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299627 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298932 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299627 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299392 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299627 1069 "q-317563" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299627 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299627 1071 "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}8 & -4 \\\\ -6 & 12\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}16 \\\\ -18\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $\\,4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,3.$ |  |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299627 1072 #uuid "d9d91921-5228-5fa0-a7a6-2fcbc61ddda4" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299627 1074 "The $2\\times 2$ matrix encodes the coefficients of $x$ and $y$, and the $2\\times 1$ vector on the right gives the constants, so the system is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}8x-4y=16 \\\\ -6x+12y=-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the first equation by $4$ and the second by $-6$ gives the simplified system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}2x-y=4 \\\\ x-2y=3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich matches the entries shown above." 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299628 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298891 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299628 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298901 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299628 1069 "q-317570" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299628 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299628 1071 "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -5 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}11 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $11$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,-7.$ |  |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299628 1072 #uuid "61031038-e22c-5885-b49a-a1823235ca68" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299628 1074 "The $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4x-5y=11 \\\\ -3x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299629 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298885 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299629 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299431 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299629 1069 "q-317582" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299629 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299629 1071 "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,-7.$ |  |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299629 1072 #uuid "b07676ec-4252-579f-89b9-78b9cf7c6870" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299629 1074 "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}0x+1y=5 \\\\ -1x+0y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}y=5 \\\\ -x=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299630 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298759 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299630 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299413 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299630 1069 "q-317583" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299630 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299630 1071 "What is the system of equations represented by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]?\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system of equations is\n\n| { | {{field-1}} | $=$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| {{field-2}} | $=$ | $\\,\\,-7.$ |  |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299630 1072 #uuid "267f94e4-48b2-5a54-9c3b-23086cc4a9c1" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299630 1074 "The  $2\\times 2$ matrix represents the coefficients of $x$ and $y,$ while the $2\\times 1$ column vector on the right-hand side represents the constants of the equations. So, we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x+0y=10 \\\\ -3x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSimplifying both equations in the system, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5x=10 \\\\ -3x+2y=-7\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299631 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299015 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299631 1069 "q-317586" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299631 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299631 1071 "Which of the following is the graph of $y=5({4}^{x})-3?$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299631 1072 #uuid "1e6ec4f9-b711-56ff-9517-409b8d594fd8" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299631 1074 "To plot the given function, we follow these steps:\n\n- We take the curve $y=5({4}^{x}).$\n\n![](images/ad/add3fbcce9c5e213fa21f8cb4744384653ef182d9cf8a94d32c05c7c5a05812e.png)\n\n- Then, vertically shift it by $3$ units down to give $y=5({4}^{x})-3.$ The point $(0,5)$ moves to $(0,2)$ and the horizontal asymptote moves from $y=0$ to $y=-3.$\n\n![](images/81/8134008472093442320629049fafa0646e0705c32a406abbf50bd90c27110ebe.png)" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299632 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299081 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299632 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299398 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299632 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299632 1069 "q-317606" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299632 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299632 1071 "A linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis. Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(u)=[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299632 1072 #uuid "8da8bcfe-6c86-5e96-b6b0-a1747142aaaf" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299632 1074 "First, we are told that $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis.\n\nComparing the $x$- and $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u),$ we note the following:\n\n- the $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u)$ are the same, while\n\n- the $x$-component of $T(u)$ is $3$ times the $x$-component of $u.$\n\nSo, we conclude that $T$ represents a stretch of scale factor $3$ in the $x$-direction. \n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299633 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299072 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299633 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299131 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299633 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299249 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299633 1069 "q-317609" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299633 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299633 1071 "A linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis. Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(u)=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} |  |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299633 1072 #uuid "9ae414af-8983-5296-9cdd-42629db05cdf" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299633 1074 "First, we are told that $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis.\n\nComparing the $x$- and $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u),$ we note the following:\n\n- the $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u)$ are the same, while\n\n- the $x$-component of $T(u)$ is $\\frac{1}{2}$ times the $x$-component of $u.$\n\nSo, we conclude that $T$ represents a stretch of scale factor $\\frac{1}{2}$ in the $x$-direction. \n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299634 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299050 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299634 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299232 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299634 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299289 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299634 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299388 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299634 1069 "q-317612" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299634 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299634 1071 "A linear transformation $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis. Given that $u=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $T(u)=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}],$ what is the standard matrix of $T?$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $T=\\,\\,$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299634 1072 #uuid "0f51d731-7249-537a-abb9-1fe5a0fa8533" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299634 1074 "First, we are told that $T$ represents a stretch along the $x$-axis or $y$-axis.\n\nComparing the $x$- and $y$-components of $u$ and $T(u),$ we note the following:\n\n- the $x$-components of $u$ and $T(u)$ are the same, while\n\n- the $y$-component of $T(u)$ is $\\sqrt{3}$ times the $y$-component of $u.$\n\nSo, we conclude that $T$ represents a stretch of scale factor $\\sqrt{3}$ in the $y$-direction. \n\nTherefore, the standard matrix of $T$ is\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299635 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298826 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299635 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298921 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299635 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299101 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299635 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299240 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299635 1069 "q-317632" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299635 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299635 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+4=7 \\\\ -2x+6z-1=8 \\\\ 7y-5z+2=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $5$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} | $6$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $9$ |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $7$ | $-5$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-5$ |  |  |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299635 1072 #uuid "cdeadc34-e7f3-5a9c-9bba-7c02bc1cee1c" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299635 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+0z=3 \\\\ -2x+0y+6z=9 \\\\ 0x+7y-5z=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299636 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298841 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299636 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299086 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299636 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299379 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299636 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299436 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299636 1069 "q-317639" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299636 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299636 1071 "The system of equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4z+x-3=7 \\\\ 2x-5y+6=1 \\\\ 3y+7z-4x+5=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $1$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $10$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $3$ | $7$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299636 1072 #uuid "2a4ab7e0-5c2e-51f8-b6d7-195279e97c0b" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299636 1074 "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+4z=10 \\\\ 2x-5y+0z=-5 \\\\ -4x+3y+7z=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299637 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298684 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299637 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298881 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299637 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298908 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299637 1069 "q-317652" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299637 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299637 1071 "Let $a=⟨5,-3,4⟩$ and $b=⟨1,2,-2⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299637 1072 #uuid "017c63a0-65df-5416-b29d-07a53e9a467a" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299637 1074 "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-2)}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{5-6-8}{1+4+4}\\,⟨1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =