calar projection of $t$ onto $u.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{u}\\,t=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299710 1072 #uuid "3704c26f-1804-5b27-a680-7d8f815d3672" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299710 1074 "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{u}\\,t & =|\\,t\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}cos\\,(\\frac{3\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299711 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298687 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299711 1069 "q-318976" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299711 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299711 1071 "Suppose $|\\,r\\,|=3\\sqrt{3}$ and the angle between vectors $r$ and $s$ is $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$ Find the scalar projection of $r$ onto $s.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{s}\\,r=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299711 1072 #uuid "bbd01580-a282-5eb8-b608-20ac603d9781" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299711 1074 "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{s}\\,r & =|\\,r\\,|\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}cos\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299712 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298755 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299712 1069 "q-318977" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299712 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299712 1071 "Let $p=⟨4,-1,1⟩$ and $q=⟨1,2,2⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299712 1072 #uuid "4084d86f-eb87-5f25-b405-7c5720bf45bf" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299712 1074 "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(4)(1)+(-1)(2)+(1)(2)}{\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4-2+2}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299713 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299354 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299713 1069 "q-318979" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299713 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299713 1071 "Let $a=⟨3,-2,1⟩$ and $b=⟨2,1,-2⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299713 1072 #uuid "aaf8f1e8-3743-57db-8cf5-200275190fd5" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299713 1074 "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(3)(2)+(-2)(1)+(1)(-2)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6-2-2}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299714 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298815 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299714 1069 "q-318981" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299714 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299714 1071 "Let $r=⟨-1,2,3⟩$ and $s=⟨2,0,0⟩.$ Find the scalar projection of $r$ onto $s.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{s}\\,r=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299714 1072 #uuid "7682317e-79ab-546a-b643-7edbcbe6f8ee" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299714 1074 "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{s}\\,r & =\\frac{r\\cdot s}{|\\,s\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{r}_{x}{s}_{x}+{r}_{y}{s}_{y}+{r}_{z}{s}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{s}_{x}^{2}+{s}_{y}^{2}+{s}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-1)(2)+(2)(0)+(3)(0)}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{\\sqrt{4}} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299715 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298774 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299715 1069 "q-318987" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299715 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299715 1071 "Let $m=⟨6,8,0⟩$ and $n=⟨0,5,12⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m-{\\text{comp}}_{m}\\,n.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m-{\\text{comp}}_{m}\\,n=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299715 1072 #uuid "b5e680fa-ce4a-56db-a90a-7d183fdb5f25" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299715 1074 "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m & =\\frac{m\\cdot n}{|\\,n\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{m}_{x}{n}_{x}+{m}_{y}{n}_{y}+{m}_{z}{n}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{n}_{x}^{2}+{n}_{y}^{2}+{n}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(6)(0)+(8)(5)+(0)(12)}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{5}^{2}+{12}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{\\sqrt{169}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{m}\\,n & =\\frac{m\\cdot n}{|\\,m\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{m}_{x}{n}_{x}+{m}_{y}{n}_{y}+{m}_{z}{n}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{m}_{x}^{2}+{m}_{y}^{2}+{m}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{8}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{40}{\\sqrt{100}} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,m-{\\text{comp}}_{m}\\,n & =\\frac{40}{13}-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{40-52}{13} \\\\  & =-\\frac{12}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299716 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299334 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299716 1069 "q-318988" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299716 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299716 1071 "Let $p=⟨9,12,0⟩$ and $q=⟨0,3,4⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p-{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p-{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299716 1072 #uuid "c6dbc91c-6749-54fc-b502-867b88fba0c5" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299716 1074 "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(9)(0)+(12)(3)+(0)(4)}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,p\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{\\sqrt{{9}^{2}+{12}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{\\sqrt{225}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p-{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{36}{5}-\\frac{12}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299717 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299074 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299717 1069 "q-318994" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299717 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299717 1071 "Compute the exact value of the definite integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}\\cdot {({x}^{3}+5)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299717 1072 #uuid "b16d83bf-12e3-5715-9420-1c293062c088" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299717 1074 "We start by changing the variable:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u & ={x}^{3}+5 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2} \\\\ \\text{d}u & =3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 6{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\,\\text{d}u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we create a table for the limits of integration using the rule $u={x}^{3}+5.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & 0 & 1 \\\\ u & 5 & 6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the integral in terms of the new variable is\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{2}\\cdot {({x}^{3}+5)}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{5}^{6}{u}^{3}\\cdot 2\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can solve it and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{6}2{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u & =2{\\int }_{5}^{6}{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\frac{{u}^{4}}{4}|}_{5}^{6} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}({6}^{4}-{5}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(1296-625) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 671 \\\\  & =\\frac{671}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299718 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298679 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299718 1069 "q-31903" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299718 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299718 1071 "Find the slope of the tangent line to the function $y=arcsec({x}^{3}-6x)$ at $x=1.$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299718 1072 #uuid "7013dfd6-3ee9-5a67-9438-689c7906b87e" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299718 1074 "The formula for the derivative of $arcsec$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsecx)=\\frac{1}{|x|\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule and the formula above, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(arcsec({x}^{3}-6x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3}-6x) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\cdot (3{x}^{2}-6) \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}-6}{|{x}^{3}-6x|\\sqrt{({x}^{3}-6x)^{2}-1}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the tangent line to the curve at $x=1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(1)\\text{ } & =\\frac{3(1)^{2}-6}{|{1}^{3}-6(1)|\\sqrt{({1}^{3}-6(1))^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-3}{|-5|\\sqrt{(1-6)^{2}-1}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{24}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\sqrt{4\\cdot 6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\cdot \\sqrt{4}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5\\cdot 2\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{10\\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{10\\sqrt{6}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3\\sqrt{6}}{60} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299719 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299326 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299719 1069 "q-319033" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299719 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299719 1071 "The initial velocity of a particle is $(6i-2j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$ Find the **exact** speed of the particle after $3$ hours if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-i+4j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.$\n\n$|v|=$\n\n{{field-1}} $\\text{km/h}.$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299719 1072 #uuid "a89b3031-0267-58bd-8159-e54ed38b6849" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299719 1074 "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=6i-2j,\\,a=-i+4j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=3\\,\\text{h},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(6i-2j)+(-i+4j)(3) \\\\  & =(6i-2j)+(-3i+12j) \\\\  & =(3\\,i+10\\,j)\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|3i+10j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{10}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+100} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{109}\\,\\text{km/h}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299720 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299008 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299720 1069 "q-319037" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299720 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299720 1071 "The initial velocity of a particle is $(2i+5j)\\,\\text{m/s}.$ Find the **exact** speed of the particle after $3$ seconds if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-3i+j)\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$\n\n$|v|=$\n\n{{field-1}} $\\text{m/s}.$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299720 1072 #uuid "d6aba2fa-7e27-5e44-94d2-64a6ae465a78" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299720 1074 "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\nu=2i+5j,\\,a=-3i+j.\n$$\n\nTherefore, after $t=3\\,\\text{s},$ the velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\  & =(2i+5j)+(-3i+j)(3) \\\\  & =(2i+5j)+(-9i+3j) \\\\  & =(-7\\,i+8\\,j)\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|v| & =|-7i+8j| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-7)^{2}+{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{113}\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299721 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299033 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299721 1069 "q-31907" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299721 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299721 1071 "Consider a system of two linear equations in two variables, represented by the matrix equation $Ax=b$ in the usual way. Given that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is invertible\n- $det(A)=0$\n- $Ax=0$ has an infinite number of solutions" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299721 1072 #uuid "1a35d343-f492-5478-a8b0-3c966904f7aa" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299721 1074 "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is false by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299722 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299380 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299722 1069 "q-319096" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299722 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299722 1071 "For the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 6\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{33}$ of the entry ${b}_{33}.$\n\n${M}_{33}=${{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299722 1072 #uuid "a4d76484-1456-5ead-bf44-7be5d6d9eb41" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299722 1074 "The minor of ${b}_{33}=6$ (third row, third column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $6$ are removed: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & ∗ \\\\ 1 & -1 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{33}=6$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{33} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-2-5 \\\\  & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299723 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298958 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299723 1069 "q-319106" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299723 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299723 1071 "For the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{23}$ of the entry ${a}_{23}.$\n\n${M}_{23}=${{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299723 1072 #uuid "d1b6b7aa-d6db-544a-a7e4-3d6fdf2e3d25" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299723 1074 "The minor of ${a}_{23}=-1$ (second row, third column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-1$ are removed: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & -1 \\\\ 0 & 6 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{23}=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{23} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot 6-(-4)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =12-0 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299724 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298890 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299724 1069 "q-319108" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299724 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299724 1071 "For the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{22}$ of the entry ${b}_{22}.$\n\n${M}_{22}=${{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299724 1072 #uuid "5fa10b30-a8e5-5b72-a911-9d9131cdfbe9" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299724 1074 "The minor of ${b}_{22}=0$ (second row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $0$ are removed: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ & -3 \\\\ ∗ & 0 & ∗ \\\\ 7 & ∗ & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{22}=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{22} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 6-(-3)\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =6-(-21) \\\\  & =6+21 \\\\  & =27.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299725 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298718 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299725 1069 "q-319110" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299725 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299725 1071 "For the matrix\n$Y=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{32}$ of the entry ${y}_{32}.$\n\n${M}_{32}=${{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299725 1072 #uuid "e7442c9a-a470-54c9-860d-582e8bf8b044" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299725 1074 "The minor of ${y}_{32}=-1$ (third row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $-1$ are removed: \n\n$$\nY=[\\begin{aligned}1 & ∗ & 5 \\\\ 3 & ∗ & 0 \\\\ ∗ & -1 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${y}_{32}=-1$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{32} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(1)\\cdot 0-3\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =0-15 \\\\  & =-15.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299726 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298862 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299726 1069 "q-319112" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299726 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299726 1071 "For the matrix\n$C=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nfind the minor ${M}_{12}$ of the entry ${c}_{12}.$\n\n${M}_{12}=${{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299726 1072 #uuid "e2f57b6a-47bc-534b-a9f4-6e1be4a28e53" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299726 1074 "The minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ (first row, second column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $2$ are removed: \n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 2 & ∗ \\\\ 0 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 7 & ∗ & 6\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${c}_{12}=2$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{12} & =\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot 6-4\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =0-28 \\\\  & =-28.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299727 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298906 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299727 1069 "q-319125" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299727 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299727 1071 "For the matrix\n$F=[\\begin{aligned}8 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & v & 4 \\\\ 5 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{13}$ of the element ${f}_{13}.$\n\n${M}_{13}=${{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299727 1072 #uuid "c5c4eca7-04b2-5aae-8b1d-a3490669714a" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299727 1074 "To evaluate the minor of ${f}_{13},$ we remove the first row and third column: \n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ & -2 \\\\ 3 & v & ∗ \\\\ 5 & 6 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${f}_{13}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{13} & =det[\\begin{aligned}3 & v \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & v \\\\ 5 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot 6-v\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =18-5v\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299038 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299728 1069 "q-319129" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299728 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299728 1071 "$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}y & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $y$ in the matrix above.\n\n$y=$\n {{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299728 1072 #uuid "e3151e3d-6c78-54a8-9112-7e12bf0e69ca" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299728 1074 "To evaluate the minor of ${f}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nF=[\\begin{aligned}y & ∗ & 1 \\\\ 2 & ∗ & 4 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}y & 1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =y\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4y-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${f}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4y-2 & =10 \\\\ 4y & =12 \\\\ y & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $y=3.$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299729 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298919 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299729 1069 "q-319138" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299729 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299729 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $x$ in the matrix above.\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299729 1072 #uuid "a1f4a024-dc0c-52c9-8ff4-2f9fe15cbc4a" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299729 1074 "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}x & ∗ & 3 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & 6 \\\\ ∗ & 8 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & =x\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-12 & =10 \\\\ 6x & =22 \\\\ x & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{11}{3}.$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299730 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299325 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299730 1069 "q-319139" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299730 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299730 1071 "$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & r & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is $15$, find the value of $r$ in the matrix above.\n\n$r=$\n {{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299730 1072 #uuid "810d97cb-2aa4-5e9c-adea-dac6f0944774" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299730 1074 "To evaluate the minor of ${b}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column: \n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & r & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}1 & r \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}] & =1\\cdot 8-r\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =8-7r.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is $15$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8-7r & =15 \\\\ -7r & =7 \\\\ r & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $r=-1.$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299731 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299421 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299731 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299460 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299731 1069 "q-319146" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299731 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299731 1071 "Given that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, find all the possible values of $p$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & p & 7 \\\\ 6 & -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn **ascending order**, the values of $p$ are\n\n$p=$ \n{{field-1}} $\\,$ and $\\,p=$\n{{field-2}}." 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299731 1072 #uuid "c0ff50c0-0f9a-524e-8769-13e8da78335f" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299731 1074 "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{11},$ we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}5 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & p & 7 \\\\ ∗ & -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}p & 7 \\\\ -8 & p-15\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =p(p-15)-7(-8) \\\\  & ={p}^{2}-15p+56.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{11}$ is $0$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{p}^{2}-15p+56 & =0 \\\\ (p-7)(p-8) & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, in ascending order, the solutions are $p=7$ and $p=8.$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299732 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299214 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299732 1069 "q-319150" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299732 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299732 1071 "Let $p=⟨3,-1,2⟩$ and $q=⟨x,1,1⟩.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299732 1072 #uuid "100a4e96-9db1-5d18-a7bd-1bd05f0073dc" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299732 1074 "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =3\\cdot x+(-1)\\cdot 1+2\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =3x+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 3x+1 & =0 \\\\ 3x & =-1 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299733 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298665 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299733 1069 "q-319162" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299733 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299733 1071 "For the matrix\n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2p & q & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4p & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & 2q\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{23}$ of the element ${b}_{23}.$\n\n${M}_{23}=${{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299733 1072 #uuid "dff6538b-44cc-5d72-9d22-4ad197bd0a51" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299733 1074 "To evaluate the minor of ${b}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}2p & q & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 5 \\\\ 6 & 7 & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${b}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{23} & =det[\\begin{aligned}2p & q \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2p & q \\\\ 6 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(2p)\\cdot 7-q\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =14p-6q.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299734 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299061 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299734 1069 "q-319164" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299734 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299734 1071 "For the matrix\n$P=[\\begin{aligned}2 & x & 3 \\\\ y & 5 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2y & x\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{23}$ of the element ${p}_{23}.$\n\n${M}_{23}=${{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299734 1072 #uuid "77631f1f-549e-50af-8aff-2f23f2d4d3b3" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299734 1074 "To evaluate the minor of ${p}_{23},$ we remove the second row and third column:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}2 & x & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗ & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2y & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${p}_{23}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{23} & =det[\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & 2y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & x \\\\ 1 & 2y\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot (2y)-x\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4y-x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299735 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299130 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299735 1069 "q-319168" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299735 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299735 1071 "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(2i+3j)\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(-6i-5j)\\,\\text{ft/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{s}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(10i+19j)\\,\\text{ft/s}.$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\text{s}$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299735 1072 #uuid "4178d7c3-09c7-532a-8e2b-23a78a693d81" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299735 1074 "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=-6i-5j,\\,v=10i+19j,\\,a=2i+3j,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ 10i+19j & =-6i-5j+(2i+3j)t \\\\ 16i+24j & =(2i+3j)t \\\\ 16i+24j & =2ti+3tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}16=2t \\\\ 24=3t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,t=8\\,\\text{s}.\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299736 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298905 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299736 1069 "q-319169" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299736 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299736 1071 "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(-2i+4j)\\,{\\text{km/h}}^{2}.$ The velocity of the particle is $(10i-8j)\\,\\text{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\text{h}.$ Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(-8i+28j)\\,\\text{km/h}.$\n\n$t=$\n{{field-1}}$\\,\\text{h}$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299736 1072 #uuid "b3d2d6eb-8dae-5f27-bfa9-9f42c7a13da3" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299736 1074 "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\nv=u+at,\n$$\n\nwhere $u$ is the initial velocity, and $a$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting \n\n$$\nu=10i-8j,\\,v=-8i+28j,\\,a=-2i+4j,\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $t,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =u+at \\\\ -8i+28j & =10i-8j+(-2i+4j)t \\\\ -18i+36j & =(-2i+4j)t \\\\ -18i+36j & =-2ti+4tj\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $i$ and $j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}-18=-2t \\\\ 36=4t\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,t=9\\,\\text{h}.\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299737 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298677 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299737 1069 "q-319171" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299737 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299737 1071 "Let $p=⟨4,1,-2⟩$ and $q=⟨1,x,3⟩.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299737 1072 #uuid "252df411-1410-5fbc-a0ba-6a3198b7a34c" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299737 1074 "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 1+1\\cdot x+(-2)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =x-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ x-2 & =0 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299738 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298666 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299738 1069 "q-319172" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299738 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299738 1071 "Let $p=⟨-2,3,4⟩$ and $q=⟨1,2,x⟩.$ Given that the scalar projection of $p$ onto $q$ is zero, find the value of $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299738 1072 #uuid "3b9e2634-f76e-5353-8b9c-ac4ebc43947e" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299738 1074 "Since $p$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $q$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\np⊥q\\,⟹\\,p\\cdot q=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & ={p}_{x}\\cdot {q}_{x}+{p}_{y}\\cdot {q}_{y}+{p}_{z}\\cdot {q}_{z} \\\\  & =-2+6+4x \\\\  & =4x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot q & =0 \\\\ 4x+4 & =0 \\\\ 4x & =-4 \\\\ x & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299739 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299025 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299739 1069 "q-319175" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299739 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299739 1071 "For the matrix\n$T=[\\begin{aligned}1 & e & f \\\\ 5 & 3d & 2 \\\\ 4 & 7 & d\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{31}$ of the element ${t}_{31}.$\n\n${M}_{31}=${{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299739 1072 #uuid "b5ce922b-4b06-539f-9202-8293bbf3e968" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299739 1074 "To evaluate the minor of ${t}_{31},$ we remove the third row and first column:\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & e & f \\\\ ∗ & 3d & 2 \\\\ 4 & ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${t}_{31}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{31} & =det[\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ 3d & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}e & f \\\\ 3d & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =e\\cdot 2-f\\cdot (3d) \\\\  & =2e-3df.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299740 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299106 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299740 1069 "q-319176" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299740 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299740 1071 "For the matrix\n$V=[\\begin{aligned}j & 1 & 3i \\\\ 2 & k & 5 \\\\ 4 & j & k\\end{aligned}],$\nfind the minor ${M}_{21}$ of the element ${v}_{21}.$\n\n${M}_{21}=${{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299740 1072 #uuid "73507977-fd56-5a33-bedf-10842b1fff67" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299740 1074 "To evaluate the minor of ${v}_{21},$ we remove the second row and first column:\n\n$$\nV=[\\begin{aligned}∗ & 1 & 3i \\\\ 2 & ∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & j & k\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${v}_{21}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{M}_{21} & =det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3i \\\\ j & k\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3i \\\\ j & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot k-(3i)\\cdot j \\\\  & =k-3ij.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299741 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298938 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299741 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298939 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299741 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299496 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299741 1069 "q-319198" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299741 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299741 1071 "Given that $c=2i-5j+k$ and $d=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],$ find $4c-3d.$\n\n$4c-3d=⟨$\n{{field-1}},\n{{field-2}},\n{{field-3}}$⟩$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299741 1072 #uuid "988a6ca5-d857-5004-9928-bb0c40ac9693" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299741 1074 "First, notice that\n\n$$\nc=2i-5j+k=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo compute $4c-3d,$ we need to perform the required operations with each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4c-3d & =4\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-3\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}12 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -23 \\\\ 10\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =⟨-4,-23,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 tru