299782 1072 #uuid "2b5cf762-3178-5e63-a1b0-8da0e65dccf1" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299782 1074 "Since we want the entry ${a}_{13}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{31}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{31} & =(-1)^{3+1}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =\\,1\\cdot (1\\cdot 4-0\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{13}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{31} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{17}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299783 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299089 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299783 1069 "q-319549" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299783 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299783 1071 "Determine the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in the inverse of a matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nif its determinant is $3.$\n\n${a}_{21}^{′}=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299783 1072 #uuid "66b7eb82-0c6f-5154-a5bd-434c9571ba55" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299783 1074 "Since we want the entry ${a}_{21}^{′}$ in ${A}^{-1},$ we need to know the value of ${c}_{12}$ in the matrix of cofactors. For this, we use the formula to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{c}_{12} & =(-1)^{1+2}|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-\\,(1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, since ${A}^{-1}=\\frac{1}{det(A)}{C}^{T},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{21}^{′} & =\\frac{1}{det(A)}\\,{c}_{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299784 1068 #e