 in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\alpha =arctan⁡(\\frac{11}{8})=0.942\\,000…\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=2\\pi -0.942\\,000≈5.34,\n$$\n\nrounded to $2$ decimal places." 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299786 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298989 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299786 1069 "q-319581" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299786 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299786 1071 "Find, **in radians**, the **exact value** of the argument of $z=8\\sqrt{3}-8\\text{i}.$\n\n**Hint**: The argument of a complex number is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$ \n\n$arg⁡(z)=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299786 1072 #uuid "e5b42c0b-e569-59e6-b7d2-a632bdfada48" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299786 1074 "Let's plot $z$ in the complex plane.\n\n![](images/78/78399e67e0ba69c1d7848a41aa5d4a5f8040fc578aab30a99f7e19ac86ece179.png)\n\nThe complex number $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant of the complex plane. Hence $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}<arg⁡(z)<2\\pi .$ \n\nIf $\\alpha $ is the angle that $z$ makes with the positive real axis, then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}tan⁡\\alpha  & =\\frac{8}{8\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ \\alpha  & =arctan\\,(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =arg⁡(z)=2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{6}=\\frac{11\\pi }{6}.\n$$" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299787 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298674 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299787 1068 #edb/ref 17592186298948 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299787 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299211 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299787 1068 #edb/ref 17592186299262 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299787 1069 "q-319591" 13194139533412 17592186045585 true] [17592186299787 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045